<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zwinger (Dresden)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1710">1710</a>–<a href="/years/1728">1728</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zwinger is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> palace complex in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a>, built from 1710 to 1728 for Augustus the Strong, Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, by the architect Matthäus Daniel Pöppelmann and the sculptor Balthasar Permoser. Designed as a festival arena with galleries and pavilions around a great courtyard, it now houses museums including the Old Masters Picture Gallery. It was rebuilt after its destruction in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zwinger-dresden.jpg" alt="Zwinger (Dresden)" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stephan Czuratis (Jazz-face) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2006-07-30_Zwinger_dresden2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
